---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout title="State of Stick Golf — A Connected Future for Golf" description="A simple, tap-connected system for golfers, golf courses, clubhouses, and leagues." eyebrow="STATE OF STICK / GOLF PRODUCT BRIEF" image="/art/golf-fairway-hero.png">
  <style is:global>
    .brief-page { --brief-green:#173b2c; --brief-ink:#172019; --brief-paper:#f5f1e7; --brief-copper:#c66b3d; --brief-muted:#53605a; background:var(--brief-paper); color:var(--brief-ink); }
    .brief-page h1,.brief-page h2,.brief-page h3,.brief-page p { max-width:none; }
    .brief-hero { padding:42px 0 58px; background:var(--brief-ink); color:#fffdf7; }
    .brief-shell { width:min(1120px,calc(100% - 44px)); margin:0 auto; }
    .brief-kicker { color:#d99a74; font:700 12px 'DM Mono',monospace; letter-spacing:.14em; }
    .brief-lockup { display:flex; align-items:center; gap:16px; padding-bottom:26px; border-bottom:1px solid #445048; }
    .brief-lockup img { width:58px; height:58px; padding:10px; background:#fffdf7; border-radius:50%; }
    .brief-lockup strong { display:block; color:#fffdf7; font-size:18px; letter-spacing:.02em; }
    .brief-lockup span { display:block; margin-top:5px; color:#bdc5bd; font:11px 'DM Mono',monospace; letter-spacing:.1em; }
    .brief-hero-grid { display:grid; grid-template-columns:1.02fr .98fr; gap:54px; align-items:center; padding-top:54px; }
    .brief-hero h1 { margin:18px 0 22px; color:#fffdf7; font-size:clamp(52px,7vw,92px); line-height:.96; letter-spacing:-.075em; }
    .brief-hero h1 em { color:#e19a70; font-style:normal; }
    .brief-hero-lead { max-width:610px; color:#d4dbd4; font-size:21px; line-height:1.45; }
    .brief-hero-image { position:relative; overflow:hidden; border:1px solid #53635a; }
    .brief-hero-image img { display:block; width:100%; height:430px; object-fit:cover; object-position:center; }
    .brief-image-caption { position:absolute; right:0; bottom:0; left:0; padding:20px; background:linear-gradient(transparent,rgba(11,22,15,.94)); color:#fffdf7; font-size:18px; font-weight:700; }
    .brief-section { padding:72px 0; }
    .brief-section.alt { background:#e7e4da; }
    .brief-section.dark { background:var(--brief-ink); color:#fffdf7; }
    .brief-section h2 { margin:10px 0 18px; font-size:clamp(38px,5vw,64px); line-height:1; letter-spacing:-.065em; }
    .brief-intro { max-width:700px; color:var(--brief-muted); font-size:20px; line-height:1.5; }
    .brief-stats { display:grid; grid-template-columns:repeat(4,1fr); gap:14px; margin-top:36px; }
    .brief-stat { min-height:190px; padding:24px; background:#fffdf7; border-top:5px solid var(--brief-copper); }
    .brief-stat strong { display:block; color:var(--brief-green); font-size:clamp(35px,4vw,56px); line-height:1; letter-spacing:-.07em; }
    .brief-stat span { display:block; margin-top:16px; font-size:16px; line-height:1.35; font-weight:700; }
    .brief-stat small { display:block; margin-top:10px; color:var(--brief-muted); font-size:12px; line-height:1.4; }
    .brief-source { margin-top:18px; color:#68716a; font:11px 'DM Mono',monospace; line-height:1.5; }
    .brief-source a { color:var(--brief-green); }
    .brief-two-col { display:grid; grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr; gap:18px; margin-top:34px; }
    .brief-card { padding:30px; background:#fffdf7; border:1px solid #d5d2c8; }
    .brief-card h3 { margin:12px 0 10px; color:var(--brief-green); font-size:28px; letter-spacing:-.045em; }
    .brief-card p { color:var(--brief-muted); font-size:17px; line-height:1.55; }
    .brief-number { color:var(--brief-copper); font:700 12px 'DM Mono',monospace; letter-spacing:.12em; }
    .brief-explainer { display:grid; grid-template-columns:.9fr 1.1fr; gap:52px; align-items:center; }
    .brief-explainer h2 { color:#fffdf7; }
    .brief-explainer > div > p { color:#d4dbd4; font-size:19px; line-height:1.55; }
    .brief-flow { display:grid; gap:10px; }
    .brief-flow-step { display:grid; grid-template-columns:58px 1fr; gap:16px; align-items:center; padding:18px; background:#fffdf7; }
    .brief-flow-step b { display:grid; place-items:center; width:46px; height:46px; border-radius:50%; background:var(--brief-copper); color:#fffdf7; font-size:20px; }
    .brief-flow-step strong { display:block; color:var(--brief-green); font-size:19px; }
    .brief-flow-step span { display:block; margin-top:4px; color:var(--brief-muted); font-size:15px; line-height:1.35; }
    .brief-proof { display:grid; grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr; gap:18px; margin-top:34px; }
    .brief-proof figure { margin:0; background:#fffdf7; }
    .brief-proof img { display:block; width:100%; height:260px; object-fit:cover; }
    .brief-proof figure:last-child img { object-fit:contain; background:#080c0a; }
    .brief-proof figcaption { padding:17px 20px; color:var(--brief-green); font-weight:700; }
    .brief-built { display:grid; grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr; gap:18px; margin-top:34px; }
    .brief-built .brief-card { border-top:5px solid var(--brief-green); }
    .brief-built .brief-card:last-child { border-top-color:var(--brief-copper); }
    .brief-ask { padding:76px 0 92px; background:var(--brief-green); color:#fffdf7; }
    .brief-ask h2 { max-width:760px; color:#fffdf7; }
    .brief-ask p { max-width:720px; color:#d5dfd6; font-size:20px; line-height:1.55; }
    .brief-button { display:inline-block; margin-top:18px; padding:16px 22px; background:#e19a70; color:#172019; font-weight:800; text-decoration:none; }
    .brief-disclaimer { padding:20px 0 36px; color:#68716a; font-size:12px; line-height:1.5; }
    @media (max-width:800px) { .brief-hero-grid,.brief-explainer { grid-template-columns:1fr; gap:30px; }.brief-stats { grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr; }.brief-hero-image img { height:320px; } }
    @media (max-width:560px) { .brief-shell { width:min(100% - 32px,1120px); }.brief-stats,.brief-two-col,.brief-proof,.brief-built { grid-template-columns:1fr; }.brief-section { padding:52px 0; }.brief-hero { padding-top:28px; }.brief-hero h1 { font-size:56px; }.brief-hero-lead { font-size:18px; }.brief-stat { min-height:auto; }.brief-lockup span { font-size:9px; } }
  </style>

  <div class="brief-page">
    <section class="brief-hero"><div class="brief-shell"><div class="brief-lockup"><img src="/brand/state-of-stick-logo.svg" alt="State of Stick mark" /><div><strong>STATE OF STICK, CO.</strong><span>GOLF / PRODUCT OWNER BRIEF</span></div></div><div class="brief-hero-grid"><div><div class="brief-kicker">THE OPPORTUNITY</div><h1>Golf is big.<br /><em>The connection is missing.</em></h1><p class="brief-hero-lead">We are building a simple layer that connects the golfer, the golf course, the clubhouse, and the league through one familiar action: tap.</p></div><div class="brief-hero-image"><img src="/art/golf-fairway-hero.png" alt="Golf fairway with a physical connected course medallion" /><div class="brief-image-caption">A physical course marker becomes a doorway to the digital experience.</div></div></div></div></section>

    <section class="brief-section"><div class="brief-shell"><div class="brief-kicker">WHY NOW / VERIFIED INDUSTRY FACTS</div><h2>This is not a small hobby market.</h2><p class="brief-intro">The market is large, active, and still changing. These numbers show why a better connection between play, courses, and communities matters.</p><div class="brief-stats"><article class="brief-stat"><strong>47.2M</strong><span>U.S. golf participants in 2024</span><small>Includes on-course and off-course participation.</small></article><article class="brief-stat"><strong>28.1M</strong><span>U.S. on-course golfers in 2024</span><small>The highest level since the Great Recession.</small></article><article class="brief-stat"><strong>500M+</strong><span>Rounds played in the U.S. in 2024</span><small>The fifth consecutive year above 500 million rounds.</small></article><article class="brief-stat"><strong>$102B</strong><span>Direct annual U.S. golf impact</span><small>The broader economic impact is $226.5B and supports 1.65M jobs.</small></article></div><p class="brief-source">Sources: <a href="https://www.ngf.org/short-game/golfs-state-of-industry-in-3-minutes/" rel="noopener">National Golf Foundation, 2024 industry overview</a>; <a href="https://rulesworkshops.usga.org/content/usga/home-page/articles/2025/03/golfs-new-narrative.html" rel="noopener">USGA, Golf’s New Narrative</a>; <a href="https://www.ngf.org/member-publication/golf-economic-impact-report-2023/" rel="noopener">NGF, 2023 Economic Impact Report</a>.</p></div></section>

    <section class="brief-section alt"><div class="brief-shell"><div class="brief-kicker">THE PROBLEM IN PLAIN ENGLISH</div><h2>Golf has places, people,<br />and activity. They are disconnected.</h2><div class="brief-two-col"><article class="brief-card"><div class="brief-number">TODAY</div><h3>The golfer carries the burden</h3><p>Scorekeeping, league details, clubhouse requests, course information, and memories are spread across different tools—or handled manually.</p></article><article class="brief-card"><div class="brief-number">THE OPENING</div><h3>Make the course easier to use</h3><p>A tap at the right physical point can show the next useful action: record a score, ask a question, contact the clubhouse, join a challenge, or see the season.</p></article></div></div></section>

    <section class="brief-section dark" id="how-it-works"><div class="brief-shell brief-explainer"><div><div class="brief-kicker">HOW IT WORKS</div><h2>One tap.<br />Four useful outcomes.</h2><p>The technology stays in the background. The golfer sees a clear, useful response at the moment it matters.</p></div><div class="brief-flow"><div class="brief-flow-step"><b>1</b><div><strong>Tap the course marker</strong><span>A flagstick, tee marker, cart, clubhouse point, or passport.</span></div></div><div class="brief-flow-step"><b>2</b><div><strong>See the right experience</strong><span>Score, course guidance, clubhouse service, event, or league action.</span></div></div><div class="brief-flow-step"><b>3</b><div><strong>Ask the golf agent</strong><span>Get grounded answers using approved course and player context.</span></div></div><div class="brief-flow-step"><b>4</b><div><strong>Carry the season forward</strong><span>Keep the passport, compete with others, and return to the course.</span></div></div></div></div></section>

    <section class="brief-section alt"><div class="brief-shell"><div class="brief-kicker">WHAT EXISTS / WHAT COMES NEXT</div><h2>There is already a foundation.<br />The next step is a real pilot.</h2><div class="brief-built"><article class="brief-card"><div class="brief-number">BUILT NOW</div><h3>A working product direction</h3><p>Golf course and hole experiences, tap-connected touchpoints, scoring, a golfer passport, portable league concepts, course discovery, API foundations, and a Durable Object round-session foundation are in the codebase.</p></article><article class="brief-card"><div class="brief-number">NEXT BUILD</div><h3>Connect the clubhouse</h3><p>Start with one course and prove the highest-value workflows: live scoring, clubhouse requests, announcements, events, AI guidance, and a season that keeps golfers coming back.</p></article></div><div class="brief-proof"><figure><img src="/art/flagstick-tap-medallion.png" alt="Physical golf flagstick tap medallion" /><figcaption>The physical doorway: tap the course.</figcaption></figure><figure><img src="/art/golf-emblems.png" alt="Green and copper golf passport emblems" /><figcaption>The portable identity: carry the season.</figcaption></figure></div></div></section>

    <section class="brief-ask"><div class="brief-shell"><div class="brief-kicker">THE ASK</div><h2>Help us choose the first course and make this useful.</h2><p>You know golf, golfers, and what a course can realistically support. We are asking you to become the product owner for this vertical: pressure-test the idea, select the first pilot, introduce the right people, and help us build the version golfers will actually use.</p><p>This is not a request to understand every technical detail. It is a request to help decide what matters first.</p><a class="brief-button" href="/operator/">Open the course pilot →</a></div></section>
    <div class="brief-shell brief-disclaimer">Market figures are third-party industry measurements. Product capabilities are a mix of implemented foundation and proposed pilot scope; the pilot is the next proof point.</div>
  </div>
</Layout>
